{
  // `tsconfig.json` has `"include": ["src"]`, so `tsc` has never looked at the
  // root-level entry points -- and nothing else does either: `npm run lint`
  // scopes to `^src/`, rollup's entry is `src/index.ts` and reaches none of
  // them, and `jest.config.cjs` sets ts-jest `isolatedModules: true`, which is
  // transpile-only. So a type error in `monitor.ts` passed every gate in this
  // repo, and the type-based guarantees `src/vehicle-db.ts` documents -- a
  // required `CheckRow` field forces a writer to supply it -- could not fire
  // against the one production writer. This config is what makes them fire.
  //
  // Narrow on purpose. Four other root paths are NOT here, measured 2026-10-11
  // by adding each one alone:
  //   get-fuel-level.ts  8 errors   debug.ts  1 error   __tests__/  5 errors
  //   scripts/           0 errors -- green today, deferred only to keep #19's
  //                                  diff to the file it is about (see #27)
  // Widening this is a follow-up, not a drive-by: a config that cannot pass
  // today would be a permanently red gate, which is the same non-gate as none.
  //
  // `monitor-fuel.ts` joined the covered set in #19. It was held out for the
  // three `TS2345` errors PR #21 fixed, and nothing else -- its whole import
  // graph was already clean, which is why it could be added by widening one
  // line rather than by a second round of fixes.
  //
  // ADDING AN ENTRY BELOW IS A TWO-FILE EDIT. `COVERED_ENTRY_POINTS` in
  // `__tests__/typecheck-gate.spec.ts` is asserted as a SET against this list,
  // so an entry added here alone turns a test you did not touch red. That is
  // the review hook, not a bug.
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "noEmit": true,
    "allowImportingTsExtensions": true
  },
  "include": ["src", "monitor.ts", "status-json.ts", "alert-backends.ts", "monitor-fuel.ts"]
}
